  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Florida has $638M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 3,462 awards with an average award size of $184K. Obligations are down 98.2% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer in Florida so far, obligating $215M. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration follows with $136M, and the Department of Homeland Security follows with $89.6M. BLUE ORIGIN, LLC is the top vendor with $99.2M, followed by AKIMA INFRASTRUCTURE PROTECTION LLC with $69.6M and VETERANS DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION, INC. with $63.1M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligations at $103M. Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation accounts for $99.2M and Security Guards and Patrol Services accounts for $80.4M. These totals are contract obligations and the FY2027 numbers are fiscal year to date, so current-year totals are partial.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the FY2027 to date total of $638M in Florida?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $215M, which is the largest single contribution to the $638M total. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration and the Department of Homeland Security added $136M and $89.6M respectively. The low fiscal year to date total also corresponds with obligations being down 98.2% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which vendors and industries account for the largest shares of Florida obligations?",
        "body": "BLUE ORIGIN, LLC is the largest vendor with $99.2M, followed by AKIMA INFRASTRUCTURE PROTECTION LLC at $69.6M and VETERANS DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION, INC. at $63.1M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction leads industries with $103M, Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation has $99.2M, and Security Guards and Patrol Services has $80.4M."
      }
    ]
  },
